## Last text from previous session

completion, the release bwrite **already retires the BLI**. My `dir_release_retire_bli` was therefore a **double `xfs_buf_item_done`** → use-after-free = the corruption. This means the **zombie-BLI-reflush theory is wrong** — the release path doesn't leave a zombie. Let me confirm line 1387 is the write-completion branch.
Confirmed: line 1320 `} else {` is the **write-completion** branch, so `xfs_buf_item_done` (retire + free BLI) runs on every release bwrite completion. **The zombie-BLI theory is refuted** — the release path correctly retires BLIs, my `dir_release_retire_bli` was a double-free (the corruption), and the **delwri-submit lead is moot** (xfs_bwrite already does the same completion). This is an important course-correction. The real loss vector: a buffer **modified (RMW) on a stale base** committed with a fresh BLI, where the base was stale because a **get_buf/non-read modify path** used evicted-but-not-re-read `b_addr` (bgen=0). Let me record this correction so the next session doesn't chase the dead leads.
The refocused angle needs the exact modify call-site that RMWs a stale (DONE=0, bgen=0) base. There's already a `P33-LOGSTALE` probe that logs when a dir buffer is **logged with XBF_DONE clear** (re-log on an invalidated/evicted base) — exactly this signal. Let me check whether it fired in the captures.
P33-LOGSTALE fired **0×** — so modifies always happen on a DONE=1 (valid) base, not an evicted one. Combined with reads-coherent, this yields a sharper, actionable hypothesis for the loss:

**The re-read-reverts mechanism**: (1) node modifies block B (adds entry X), commits → BLI in AIL, `b_addr={...,X}`, DONE=1, but **not yet written to disk**; (2) grant_evict's prior-tenure/grant-stale override force-clears XBF_DONE on B even though it's `in_ail`-undestaged (it treats the undestaged flag as a stale-prior-tenure "false positive"); (3) a subsequent read of the now-DONE=0 B re-fetches from **disk** (which lacks X) → `b_addr` reverts to `{...}`; (4) the still-in-AIL BLI is written with the reverted `b_addr` → **X durably lost**. This fits everything: reads coherent, BLI properly retired, bgen=0 at the clobber, no P33-LOGSTALE.

The fix direction: the evict's prior-tenure/grant-stale overrides must **never clear XBF_DONE on a buffer that is `in_ail && undestaged`** (committed-but-unwritten *this-tenure* work) — only genuinely-durable prior-tenure buffers. I've recorded this as the lead.

I'm at the ccloop relay boundary, so wrapping up this sub-step.

